{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419794","formula":"Mg₄(Mg₃Al₉)O₄[Si₃Al₉O₃₆]","hill":"Al18Mg7O40Si3","elements":["O","Mg","Al","Si"],"composition":{"O":40.0,"Al":18.0,"Mg":7.0,"Si":3.0},"names":{"en":"Sapphirine","ru":"Сапфирин","uk":"Сапфірин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sapphirine is a rare mineral, a silicate of magnesium and aluminium, with the chemical formula (Mg,Al)8(Al,Si)6O20 (with iron as a major impurity). Named for its sapphire-like colour, sapphirine is primarily of interest to researchers and collectors: well-formed crystals are treasured and occasionally cut into gemstones. Sapphirine has also been synthesized for experimental purposes via a hydrothermal process.","ru":"Сапфирин — минерал, алюмосиликат магния из класса силикатов, давший название группе и надгруппе минералов. Химическая формула Mg4(Mg3Al9)O4[Si3Al9O36]. Кристаллическая структура цепочечная.","uk":"Сапфірин (рос. сапфирин; англ. sapphirine; нім."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419794","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sapphirine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%84%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%84%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sapphirine_(Madagascar).jpg","license":"Copyrighted free use"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q191310","formula":"MgAl₂O₄","names":{"en":"Spinel","ru":"Шпинель","uk":"Шпінель